e snapshot tooling existed, installed btrfs-progs, built and formatted a loopback btrfs image, and mounted it as /srv/data with a 'data' subvolume.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Snapshot persistence across mounts (fstab)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-55fecf467f5b4cd9\",\"cmd-864dd5e9150a44b5\"],\"summary\":\"Added an /etc/fstab entry using loop,subvol=data and verified a clean umount/mount -a round trip mounts /srv/data correctly.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline application data and snapshot captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-47ae31547d9f4d41\",\"cmd-67530fadbf3a4ec0\"],\"summary\":\"Wrote config.yaml, accounts.csv, audit.log to /srv/data/app, recorded sha256 checksums, then created read-only btrfs snapshot ID 257 of the data subvolume.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Directory modified after snapshot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1bdddc168d684e3d\"],\"summary\":\"Deleted accounts.csv, overwrote config.yaml, appended to audit.log, and added malware.txt; checksums confirm divergence from baseline.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Exact restoration of earlier snapshot content\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fe1545cb2bd544e2\"],\"summary\":\"Deleted mutated subvolume, created new writable snapshot from the read-only baseline snapshot; sha256 checksums of restored files exactly match the original baseline (cmd-47ae31547d9f4d41), malware.txt is gone, config.yaml/accounts.csv content restored.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7142a558685b43e0\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 34abf93f-a408-4f81-a5f9-7bb344ff8724, confirmed /srv/data mounted with restored, checksum-matching data, and fstab entry present.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0ead2acdcff9457e\"],\"summary\":\"Issued backgrounded 'sleep 1; reboot' so the acknowledgement returned before the node disconnected.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving genuine restart (node1)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3d16a344c2db4ad3\",\"cmd-cbc706